\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Limitation breakdown for the 55 \textit  {not\_detectable} instances. Analysis-engine limitations (L1--L3, 21 cases) are precision losses internal to the abstract interpreter that no developer annotation can recover. Annotation-model limitations (L4--L5, 34 cases) are cases the interpreter \emph  {would} distinguish given the right annotation, but the current model cannot express that annotation (L4) or only with bug awareness (L5).}}{30}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rq1-limitations}{{5}{30}{Limitation breakdown for the 55 \textit {not\_detectable} instances. Analysis-engine limitations (L1--L3, 21 cases) are precision losses internal to the abstract interpreter that no developer annotation can recover. Annotation-model limitations (L4--L5, 34 cases) are cases the interpreter \emph {would} distinguish given the right annotation, but the current model cannot express that annotation (L4) or only with bug awareness (L5)}{figure.caption.22}{}}
